 "poem": "183, The Commencement of the Composition of\nI. Adieu! Some Maidens have disappeared,\nLike stars whose brightness shall not return; love\nTo give us thee, on earth thy honour,\nAnd, like thee, in heaven to shine again:\nWho silent foot hath trod our muddy\nFootsteps by the current's revell'd river,\nBy whom we never know her mistress be,\nNor yet live as if she had forgotten:\nFarewell - let all happy thought depart,\nO Lady Timon, to serve Thy Father,\nThy soul to pleasure Thou canst impart,",
